data.content:
Here's the output:

```
{"Name":"Alice","Age":30}
```

The key is `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` — added in .NET 9 and available out of the box. Since your record uses lowercase constructor parameters (`name`, `age`), the policy converts them to `Name` and `Age` in the JSON.

**Program.cs:**

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("Alice", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string name, int age);
```
